    "Header": "Identifying cellular and spatial composition of the tumor microenvironment (TME) is vital for interpretation of disease origin, progression, prognosis and treatment options.\n\nImaging Mass Cytometry™ (IMC™) technology is a spatial biology imaging technique that enables deep characterization of the TME. Here, a whole tissue section of Stage 3 ccRCC was acquired on a Hyperion™ XTi Imaging System using Tissue Mode. This imaging mode generates a high-quality scan of the entire tissue section in a matter of hours. The spatial relationships of immune subsets relative to tumor cells, vasculature and stromal components were resolved, uncovering distinct patterns of immune infiltration and congregation. A large component of tumor and stromal cells is observed with multiple TLS-like structures found within tumor cells and tumor margins.\n\n42-parameter panel used: combines the Human Immuno-Oncology IMC Panel, 31 Antibodies (PN 201509) and individual antibodies.\n\nTime to acquire: 2 hours 52 minutes",
